# {{ m }}

This directory contains a self-contained C99 state-machine runtime. Put your application in `app.c`; regenerate the machine files from the DSL when model behavior changes. The generated program has no Python or third-party runtime dependency.

**Generated files:** Use `machine.h` and its public functions for integration. `machine.c` are generated implementation files. This guide and `README_zh.md` describe the same API. The machine type is opaque statically sized storage: read it only through the functions below. {% if model.has_regions %}This model declares regions, so it has no single current state; read its position as a configuration value.{% else %}This model declares no regions, so its position is always one current state.{% endif %} Follow [Quick Start](#quick-start), then [Integration](#integration), [Recovery](#recovery), [Configuration values](#configuration) and [Build](#build).

