```

```bash
cc -std=c99 -Wall -Wextra -pedantic -O2 machine.c app.c -lm -o app
./app
```

These commands target a POSIX hosted toolchain. See Build for Windows, CMake and no-heap integration. On each later tick, refresh `data.inputs` (or read the device inside the provider), then call the same cycle entry. Stop after `is_ended()` becomes true. Keep the instance, callback tables and application data alive for the whole run.

